WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.350
We're not actively rooting for any of these
movies to fail - but there's something about

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.060
each of them that carries the whiff of an
inevitable bomb.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:11.660
We may be wrong, but thankfully for us, we're
not the studio executives whose jobs depend

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.420
on these turkeys turning a profit.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.320
Here are our predictions for the biggest box
office bombs of 2020.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:22.400
Matthew McConaughey's career rebirth, dubbed
the McConaissance, has been good for the actor,

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.060
and great for film and TV fans.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.960
However, despite the praise, box office results
and even an Academy Award win for Dallas Buyers

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:34.160
Club, this is still the same guy who recently
signed on to star in Serenity, The Beach Bum,

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:35.140
and The Dark Tower.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.200
"Death always wins.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.260
That's the deal."

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.980
McConaughey has come far, but he's still prone
to headlining duds, and the forthcoming The

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.500
Gentlemen looks to be one of them.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:51.240
With Guy Ritchie at the helm, McConaughey
leads a stacked cast including Charlie Hunnam,

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.920
Colin Farrell, and Hugh Grant.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.880
The British/American co-production is about
a British drug lord who tries to sell his

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.500
empire to a dynasty of Oklahoma billionaires.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:03.880
Sounds good, but in addition to McConaughey's
spotty box office, there's the release date:

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:08.760
January 24, 2020, just one week after Dolittle
and Bad Boys for Life.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.340
A movie doesn't have to be high-profile to
be a bomb.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:13.340
Take Run, for example.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.600
It's scheduled for release on January 24,
2020, and we barely know a thing about it.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.200
We don't even have a trailer for it.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:24.400
All we know is it stars Sarah Paulson, and
it's about a teenage girl who has been raised

00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:28.240
in total isolation by her mother, and then
discovers that her mother has been hiding

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:29.240
a sinister secret.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:33.159
That makes it sound like it could be interesting,
especially since it's created by the team

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:34.680
that made the underrated Searching.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.200
Unfortunately, there's been almost no promotion
behind it, which would seem to indicate that

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:43.060
Lionsgate doesn't have much confidence in
the film, and is trying to quietly unload

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.930
it during one of the winter dump months.

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:49.920
Lionsgate has had a very successful 2019 with
John Wick 3, so maybe they just want Run to

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.300
quietly saunter away while they plot their
next blockbuster.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:57.820
"Long live the king."

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:01.520
Sonic the Hedgehog crashing and burning seems
guaranteed at this point.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.660
But what else can you expect when reactions
to the first trailer were so bad?

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:09.040
It was such a mess that director Jeff Fowler
pledged to redesign the character to please

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:09.540
fans.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:13.480
This massive undertaking pushed the film back
from its original release date of November

00:02:13.489 --> 00:02:20.159
8, 2019 to February 14, 2020, and no doubt
added some zeroes to its reported $90 million

00:02:20.159 --> 00:02:21.159
budget.

00:02:21.159 --> 00:02:24.560
With that costly redesign, it's hard not to
wonder whether Paramount should have taken

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:27.840
a loss on a modest dud instead of the massive
bomb we're now expecting.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:32.120
With a few notable exceptions, video game
adaptations aren't exactly blessed with a

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:35.160
great track record when it comes to box office
performance.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.600
Sonic the Hedgehog seems unlikely to fix that.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:42.030
In fact, we expect the fastest thing on land
to speed right out of theaters within a few

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:42.520
weeks.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:48.380
Fantasy Island was a cheesy 1970s TV show
starring Ricardo Montalban as the host of

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:49.800
a magical island resort.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.720
2020's Fantasy Island is a big-screen update
starring Michael Peña, which, based on the

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:59.519
trailer, turns the resort into a torture paradise
similar to movies like Saw and Hostel.

00:02:59.519 --> 00:03:03.799
The studio behind the movie, Blumhouse, has
more or less earned our trust over the years,

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:08.400
but turning a 1970s TV hit into a gory horror
movie seems like a stretch.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:12.659
It's difficult to imagine fans of the original
show turning out for this, while modern horror

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.240
fans seem very unlikely to even be familiar
with the source material.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:21.780
Fantasy Island is set for release on February
14, 2020, so maybe it'll satisfy young lovers'

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:26.040
bloodlust by showing pretty people getting
hacked to pieces over Valentine's Day weekend.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:30.349
Though with the recent success of supernatural
and high-brow horror films like It Follows,

00:03:30.349 --> 00:03:34.370
A Quiet Place, and Hereditary, we can't help
but wonder if there's even an audience for

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.420
this type of torture-driven horror anymore.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:40.560
Even if there is, will Fantasy Island be the
movie that they show up in droves for?

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:45.020
Comic book movies are often big business at
the box office, but most of those hits have

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:46.700
come from Marvel or DC.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:52.140
On March 13, 2020, Sony is taking a risk on
a less well-known character from Valiant Comics

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.160
named Bloodshot.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:58.249
In Bloodshot, a murdered soldier seeks revenge
after being reanimated with superpowers.

00:03:58.249 --> 00:04:02.809
Bloodshot has the ability to heal instantly,
and he's seeking vengeance against those who

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:05.909
"killed" him before he was re-birthed by an
evil corporation.

00:04:05.909 --> 00:04:10.920
Basically, he's like a mix between Captain
America, the Punisher, Wolverine and Robocop.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:15.040
Despite having a pretty effective trailer,
there's nothing about Bloodshot that screams

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:15.540
"must see."

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:21.320
And as summer 2019 taught us, if your blockbuster
movie isn't must-see, moviegoers won't bother,

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.040
especially with so many other entertainment
options out there.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:28.720
Sony may be hoping that star Vin Diesel will
make up for Bloodshot's lack of name recognition.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:33.690
But despite being 2017's top-grossing actor,
Diesel's box office is mostly predicated on

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:38.170
playing alongside an ensemble as he does in
the Fast and the Furious franchise, and Guardians

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:38.940
of the Galaxy.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:43.480
While Bloodshot looks likely to bomb, Diesel
can take solace knowing Fast &amp; Furious 9 will

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:46.200
be coming out a few months later with his
friends.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.120
"I don't got friends.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.120
I got family."

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:54.640
We predicted that The New Mutants would bomb
in 2019, and then it was delayed into 2020.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:55.680
Who saw that coming?

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.580
But everything we said still holds true.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:02.680
The New Mutants was originally scheduled to
be released on April 13, 2018, but was pushed

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:04.600
back to August 2, 2019.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:10.080
Following Disney's purchase of Fox, it was
pushed back again, this time to April 3, 2020.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:14.580
It doesn't help that the X-Men franchise is
in a bad way following Dark Phoenix, the final

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:17.660
film in the previous trilogy and the biggest
bomb in the series.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:22.160
Even under the best of circumstances, it would
be hard for The New Mutants to follow that.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:25.930
At this point, the studio might be better
served cutting their losses, dropping The

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.990
New Mutants onto Disney+ and crossing their
fingers.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:33.990
As is, The New Mutants may surpass Dark Phoenix's
record as the financial low point in the X-Men

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:34.700
franchise.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:35.660
On the bright side?

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:37.880
At least nobody is expecting anything different.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:43.360
Disney had one of the most successful years
ever in 2019, but Artemis Fowl doesn't feature

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:48.010
Jedi Knights, Marvel superheroes, or CG-animated
characters from Disney classics.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:52.360
It's a Disney branded live-action film that
has more in common with Disney's other live-action

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:54.660
movies, which don't tend to be quite as ground-breaking.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:01.200
Tommorowland only made $209 million worldwide
on a $190 million budget in 2015.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:08.460
A Wrinkle in Time mustered a measly $132 million
in 2018 against a $103 million budget.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:14.370
The Nutcracker and the Four Realms made a
mere $173 million worldwide against a $120

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.180
million budget.

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:19.160
Even the once-successful Pirates of the Caribbean
franchise is a sinking ship.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:22.780
Artemis Fowl is following in these footsteps,
and may do even worse.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:27.080
Based on the best-selling novel series, the
film follows a young, genius criminal mastermind

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:29.940
who becomes locked in an epic battle against
evil fairies.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:33.520
Disney probably hoped that this story would
be its Harry Potter, and it certainly seems

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:36.200
packed with fantasy and franchise potential.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:41.430
However, The House of Mouse moved Artemis
Fowl back from its original August 2019 release

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:43.880
to the more competitive summer date of May
29.

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:47.640
That could mean that the studio is feeling
confident or that it hopes to just get it

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.120
out of the way early in the summer.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:53.040
One way or another, Disney may have to sell
a lot of Baby Yoda merchandise to make up

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.800
for all the money Artemis Fowl seems likely
to lose.

00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:00.620
For the second time in four years, moviegoers
will be getting a new Ghostbusters movie.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:05.020
Ironic, considering we had to wait 27 years
for a new Ghostbusters in 2016.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:10.900
Fans didn't show up for that one, which made
a hefty-yet-disappointing $229 million worldwide

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:13.740
against a $144 million budget.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.160
Numbers like that mean one thing in Hollywood:
no sequel.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:22.280
Ghostbusters: Afterlife isn't a sequel to
the 2016 Ghostbusters, but to the 1984 original.

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:26.180
While details are sketchy, the new Ghostbusters
will essentially be the third film in the

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:30.900
original Ghostbusters franchise, with Bill
Murray, Dan Aykroyd, Sigourney Weaver, Annie

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:33.590
Potts, and Ernie Hudson reprising their roles.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:38.090
Joining their ranks are Paul Rudd, one of
the most bankable names in comedy, with Academy

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:43.030
Award-nominated director Jason Reitman, son
of original Ghostbusters director Ivan Reitman,

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:43.760
taking the reins.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:45.340
So why does this look like a bomb?

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:46.960
Well, film fans are fickle.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:51.000
Thirty-one years will have passed since the
last film in this timeline, Ghostbusters II,

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.200
was released to poor reviews in 1989.

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:54.980
Is there still a huge audience there?

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:55.640
Maybe.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:59.800
Ghostbusters seems like a beloved franchise
that's been passed down through the generations,

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:02.580
but the same could be said about Terminator
and Terminator 2.

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:07.580
Terminator: Dark Fate, released in 2019 as
a direct sequel, probably killed the franchise.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:10.540
Ghostbusters: Afterlife could meet a similar
fate on July 10.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:12.660
Eddie Murphy was huge at his peak.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:17.160
In addition to saving Saturday Night Live,
his starring role in Beverly Hills Cop saw

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:22.480
the film open in more theaters nationwide
than Indiana Jones and Ghostbusters in 1984.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:26.440
What's more, Beverly Hills Cop wound up topping
both in total final grosses.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:30.080
That's an incredible achievement, but that
was also 35 years ago.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:35.040
Despite receiving some of the best reviews
of his career for Dolemite Is My Name in 2019,

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:38.500
Eddie Murphy is a long way away from his box
office glory days.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:42.160
That said, he's hoping to change that with
a sequel to one of his biggest box office

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:45.320
hits from that era, 1988's Coming to America.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:50.079
In the original, Murphy plays a pampered African
prince who goes undercover in Queens to find

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:50.580
a wife.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:56.020
The original was a massive success, earning
returns of $288 million worldwide.

00:08:56.020 --> 00:09:00.760
Those would be huge numbers for a comedy today,
but can Coming 2 America come even close to

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:02.920
flying that high when it arrives on August
7?

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:04.079
It seems doubtful.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:05.920
For one, there's the time factor.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:09.760
Thirty-two years will have passed since Coming
To America first graced our screens.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:14.130
There's also the fact that Murphy's box office
clout has been trending downwards for a while.

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:17.380
Prince Akeem's return sadly seems likely to
continue that trend.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:23.000
On December 18, 2020, Warner Bros. hopes to
mine holiday season box office gold with an

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.940
adaptation of Frank Herbert's beloved book
series Dune.

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:30.540
Dune has sold millions of copies and may be
the greatest sci-fi novel of all time.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:34.940
But all of that has very little to do with
how successful a film adaptation is, particularly

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.240
during the end of the year.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:40.570
His Dark Materials is a pretty popular fantasy
novel series, but The Golden Compass barely

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:42.360
broke even in 2007.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:46.780
Mortal Engines sold plenty of books, but the
film couldn't sell tickets, and bombed big

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:47.280
time.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.180
And do we even need to mention John Carter?

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:53.560
Based on the Edgar Rice Burroughs Barsoom
stories, John Carter is one of the biggest

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:54.220
bombs ever.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:58.200
For every Lord of the Rings, Harry Potter,
or Game of Thrones, there are numerous other

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.580
sci-fi and fantasy stories that should have
stayed on the printed page.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:04.500
This isn't the first time Dune has been on
the big screen, either.

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:10.240
David Lynch's Dune died a horrible death in
1984, earning $30 million worldwide against

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:11.720
a $40 million budget.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.139
"I must not fear.

00:10:13.139 --> 00:10:15.199
Fear is the mind killer.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:18.500
Fear is the little death that brings total
obliteration.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:20.260
I will face my fear."

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:26.320
New Dune director Denis Villenueve's last
movie, Blade Runner 2049, tanked in 2017.

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:31.820
High-concept sci-fi is always risky, and Dune's
box office seems all but certain to lack spice.

